---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';

const L = site.legal;
const entity = L.entityName || '[Registered business name]';
const address = L.address || '[Registered address]';
const email = site.email || '[your@email]';
const goName = L.grievanceOfficerName || '[Grievance Officer name]';
const goEmail = L.grievanceOfficerEmail || site.email || '[grievance@email]';
const analytics = Boolean(site.plausibleDomain);
---
<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How evalkeen collects, uses and protects personal data when you visit our website, contact us or work with us."
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how {entity} ("evalkeen", "we", "us") collects, uses and protects personal data when
    you visit this website, contact us, book a walkthrough or work with us. We follow India's Digital Personal Data
    Protection Act, 2023 and the rules made under it.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    evalkeen builds AI automations for service businesses, such as WhatsApp assistants, call handling and follow-up
    systems. For personal data covered by this policy, we are the Data Fiduciary.
  </p>
  <p>{entity}, {address}. Email: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a></p>

  <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
  <h3>When you contact us</h3>
  <p>
    If you message us on WhatsApp, call us or email us, we receive the details you share: your name, phone number,
    email address, business name and the contents of your message.
  </p>
  <h3>When you book a walkthrough</h3>
  <p>
    Our booking page is run by a third-party scheduling service. It collects your name, email address, phone number
    (if you give it), the time you choose and any notes you add, and shares them with us.
  </p>
  <h3>When you browse this website</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Our hosting provider keeps standard server logs, such as IP address, browser type and pages requested, for security and reliability.</li>
    {analytics ? (
      <li>We use Plausible Analytics to count visits. It does not use cookies and does not collect personal data that identifies you.</li>
    ) : (
      <li>We do not use advertising or tracking cookies.</li>
    )}
    <li>
      Demo videos are hosted on YouTube or Loom. Nothing from those services loads until you press play. Once you do,
      they may set cookies and collect data under their own privacy policies.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>This website has no forms and no account sign-up. We do not buy personal data or collect it from data brokers.</p>

  <h2>3. Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to your enquiry and talk about your requirements.</li>
    <li>To schedule and hold walkthroughs and meetings.</li>
    <li>To send you proposals, agreements and invoices if you choose to work with us.</li>
    <li>To deliver and support the services we agree on.</li>
    <li>To keep this website secure and working.</li>
    <li>To meet legal, tax and accounting obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We process this data based on the consent you give when you contact us or book a call, or for legitimate uses
    allowed by law, such as performing a contract you asked for or meeting a legal obligation. We will not send you
    marketing messages unless you agree, and you can ask us to stop at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell or rent personal data. We share it only with service providers who help us run the business, such as:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>website hosting,</li>
    <li>scheduling, email and messaging providers (including WhatsApp, operated by Meta),</li>
    <li>video hosting (YouTube, Loom),</li>
    <li>accounting and payment providers, if you become a client.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose data if the law requires it, or to protect our rights or the safety of others. Some of these
    providers store data outside India. Where they do, we use reputable providers and only share what is needed.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Data we handle for our clients</h2>
  <p>
    When we build an assistant or automation for a client (for example, a clinic or a consultancy), it handles personal
    data of that client's own customers, such as enquiries, appointment details or screening answers.
  </p>
  <div class="box">
    <p>
      For that data, our client is the Data Fiduciary and we act as their Data Processor. We process it only on our
      client's instructions and under a written agreement. Where possible, it is stored in the client's own accounts
      (such as their Google Sheet or CRM), not ours. Messages may pass through the messaging and AI service providers
      named in that agreement so the assistant can reply.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are a customer of one of our clients and have a question about your data, please contact that business
      directly. We will help them respond.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep enquiry and meeting data for as long as needed to respond and follow up, and for up to 12 months after our
    last contact if we do not start working together. Client and billing records are kept for as long as the law
    requires. After that, we delete or anonymise the data.
  </p>

  <h2>7. How we protect it</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable security measures, including access controls, encrypted connections and limiting access to people
    who need it. No system is completely secure, but if a data breach affects you, we will inform you and the
    authorities as the law requires.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>tell you what personal data we hold about you and how we use it,</li>
    <li>correct, complete or update it,</li>
    <li>erase it, where we no longer need to keep it,</li>
    <li>withdraw consent you gave earlier (this does not affect processing already done),</li>
    <li>nominate someone to exercise these rights on your behalf if you die or become unable to.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To use any of these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${goEmail}`}>{goEmail}</a>. We may ask you to confirm your
    identity first. If you are outside India, you may have similar rights under your local law, and you can contact us
    the same way.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our services are meant for businesses and this website is not directed at anyone under 18. We do not knowingly
    collect personal data from children. If you believe a child has sent us personal data, contact us and we will
    delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will always be on this page, with its effective
    date at the top. If a change materially affects how we use your data, we will tell you where we can.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Grievance Officer and contact</h2>
  <p>For questions, requests or complaints about your personal data, contact our Grievance Officer:</p>
  <div class="box">
    <p>{goName}<br />{entity}, {address}<br />Email: <a href={`mailto:${goEmail}`}>{goEmail}</a></p>
  </div>
  <p>
    We will respond within the time required by law. If you are not satisfied with our response, you may complain to
    the Data Protection Board of India.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
